# cargo's build directory -- `just dsrs serve` builds `target/release/quizd.exe` here. The corpus,
# templates and assets are embedded, so that one file IS the deployment and has no business in the
# repo. Cargo.lock IS checked in: this crate builds a binary, so the exact dependency versions the
# numbers in RESULTS.md were measured against are part of the record.
/target/

# flamegraphs and profile output, if anything is ever pointed at this
/*.svg
/perf.data*

# Kept as an explicit re-include. These are askama SOURCE templates, compiled into the binary at
# build time, not build output -- this negation is what protected them back when these apps lived in
# the bridge-bidding-system notes repo, whose root ignores `*.html` because there every root .html
# IS a BML build artifact. This repo's root has no such rule, so the line is a no-op here; it stays
# so the templates survive if the app is ever vendored back under a repo that does.
!/templates/*.html
